{"tool_name":"bamtocov","contents":["bioconda","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"bamtocov","version":"2.10.0","home":"https://github.com/telatin/bamtocov","license":"MIT","summary":"Extract coverage information from BAM files, supporting stranded and physical coverage and streams.","identifiers":["biotools:bamtocov","doi:10.3390/bioengineering8050059"],"description":"A collection of tools to extract coverage information from BAM and CRAM files,\nsupporting target (BED, GFF) and reporting the output in bedGraph (BED) or WIG format.\n\nThe suite includes:\n- bamtocov: fast BAM/CRAM to coverage converter\n- covtotarget: extract coverage for specific targets\n","build":{"number":0,"run_exports":[null]},"requirements":{"build":[null,null,"nim"],"host":["zlib","pcre","htslib >=1.10"],"run":null},"source_url":"https://github.com/telatin/bamtocov/archive/v2.10.0.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["covtotarget --help","covtotarget --version | grep 2.10.0","bamtocov --version | grep 2.10.0"]},"recipe_maintainers":["telatin"]},"biotools":{"id":"bamtocov","home":"https://telatin.github.io/bamtocov/","license":"MIT","summary":"Tools to extract coverage informations from BAM (and CRAM) files, based on the covtobed algorithm that supports stranded coverage and physical coverage, input from streams and uses a memory-efficient algorithm.","addition_date":"2022-01-25T09:42:42.478699Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:31:24.841052Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"version":["2.5.0","2.7.0","2.8.0"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:bamtocov","credit":[{"name":"Giovanni Birolo","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0160-9312","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"name":"Andrea Telatin","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7619-281X","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://github.com/telatin"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Annotation track","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3002"},"format":[{"term":"BED","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3003"}]},{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1383"},"format":[{"term":"BAM","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2572"},{"term":"CRAM","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3462"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Sequence alignment conversion","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0260"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Annotation track","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3002"},"format":[{"term":"WIG","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3005"},{"term":"bedgraph","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3583"}]}]}],"name":"bamtocov","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"telatin","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btac125","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: Many genomics applications require the computation of nucleotide coverage of a reference genome or the ability to determine how many reads map to a reference region. Results: BamToCov is a toolkit for rapid and flexible coverage computation that relies on the most memory efficient algorithm and is designed for integration in pipelines, given its ability to read alignment files from streams. The tools in the suite can process sorted BAM or CRAM files, allowing the user to extract coverage information via different filtering approaches and to save the output in different formats (BED, Wig or counts). The BamToCov algorithm can also handle strand-specific and/or physical coverage analyses.","authors":[{"name":"Birolo G."},{"name":"Telatin A."}],"citationCount":11,"date":"2022-05-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"BamToCov: An efficient toolkit for sequence coverage calculations"},"note":"Bioinformatics Application note on BamToCov","pmcid":"PMC9048650","pmid":"35199151","version":"1.0"},{"doi":"10.1101/2021.11.12.466787","note":"Preprint hosted by biorXiv","type":["Method"]}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"bamtocov","home":"https://bio.tools/bamtocov","license":"MIT","version":["